# Model profile (shell syntax): one LLM a run can name with `model:` in its
# spec (configs/runs/). Immutable once a run uses it; make a -v2 to change it.
# Download its weights on coe-hpc1 with `make llm-fetch PROFILE=qwen3.6-27b-fp8-v1 LLM_PARTS=model`.

# llm_serve.sh starts: vllm (the pinned server in configs/llm/vllm.env) or fake.
LLM_SERVER=vllm

# Qwen3.6-27B, Qwen's own FP8 checkpoint (Apache-2.0, 30.9 GB of safetensors),
# pinned to a Hub commit. Dense, 64 layers; only 16 keep a per-token KV cache
# (4 KV heads x 256 dims, about 64 KiB per token), the other 48 a fixed state.
# On an A100 vLLM runs FP8 weight-only through its Marlin kernel; an H100 runs FP8 natively.
MODEL_ID=Qwen/Qwen3.6-27B-FP8
MODEL_REVISION=a56219b8202864dc6d3e565be5ff1eea01f54cb4
MODEL_DIR=Qwen3.6-27B-FP8@a56219b8

# Server settings.
# - 16384 tokens and 0.90, as in qwen2.5-coder-7b-v1, so the two profiles differ
#   only in the model. On a 40 GB A100 that leaves about 5-6 GB for the cache.
# - --language-model-only skips the vision encoder.
# - Thinking is off for every request, so a reply is the program, not reasoning,
#   within the same LLM_MAX_TOKENS as the 7B profile.
# - top_p 0.8 is Qwen's setting for non-thinking mode; the checkpoint's defaults
#   (top_p 0.95, top_k 20) are for thinking mode. top_k 20 still comes from them.
#   OpenEvolve sends only temperature and max_tokens. Qwen also suggests
#   presence_penalty 1.5, which vLLM can't set server-side and OpenEvolve 0.4.0 doesn't send.
# - --max-num-seqs 32: before sizing its cache, vLLM sets aside a test cache with
#   one block per request it may run at once (default 256). For this model a
#   block is 784 tokens and 49 MiB, so 256 needed 12.25 GiB with 10.6 GiB free
#   on an A100, and the server failed to start (job 114320). Memory allows far
#   fewer than 32 full-length requests at once anyway.
# The JSON values must contain no spaces: llm_serve.sh splits VLLM_SERVE_ARGS on spaces.
CONTEXT_TOKENS=16384
VLLM_SERVE_ARGS="--max-model-len ${CONTEXT_TOKENS} --gpu-memory-utilization 0.90 --max-num-seqs 32 --language-model-only --default-chat-template-kwargs {\"enable_thinking\":false} --override-generation-config {\"top_p\":0.8}"

# Request defaults the resolver writes into OpenEvolve's llm section.
LLM_TEMPERATURE=0.7
LLM_MAX_TOKENS=4096
LLM_TIMEOUT_S=300
